ServiceNow ITSM Foundations — Service Catalog & Request Management

One-line summary: Built and tested an end-to-end service request workflow in ServiceNow's Service Catalog, from catalog item creation through fulfillment.

Overview:

This project is part of the ITSM Foundations track. The goal was to simulate how an IT department lets employees request services (like new hardware, software access, or account changes) through a self-service catalog — and how that request routes through approval and fulfillment on the back end.
[Add 1-2 sentences here on the specific scenario you built, e.g., "I built a catalog item for requesting a new laptop, including manager approval and IT fulfillment steps."]

Environment & Tools:

Platform: ServiceNow Personal Developer Instance (PDI)
Module: Service Catalog / Request Management
Other tools: none — browser only


What I Did:

Created a new catalog item in the Service Catalog ([Apple MacBook Pro 15'])
Configured variables to capture request details ([e.g., device type, justification, urgency])
Set up a workflow/approval step so requests route to [the requester's manager] before fulfillment
Tested the request as an end user — submitted the catalog item and tracked it through the request queue and manuelly approved
Verified the request reached the correct fulfillment/assignment group and closed out correctly

